    <p>
      <b>Algorithms</b>
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>OUTPUT block with no inputs.</li>
      <li>The native runtime derives k from f0, f1, and max(t1, 0.001).</li>
      <li>The manifest k parameter is visual/configuration metadata; the native handler computes the sweep rate.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <b>Equation or Rule</b>
    </p>
    <latex>y = amp\,\sin\left(2\pi\left(f_0 t + \frac{1}{2} k t^2\right)\right)</latex>
    <p>
      <b>Extended Capabilities</b>
    </p>
    <p>This page describes the native runtime behavior observed in the module C++ sources. Declared phases indicate when the simulation engine calls the block.</p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
